---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Funerals we arrange', url: '/funeral-services/' },
  { name: 'Cremation', url: '/funeral-services/cremation/' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Cremation Funerals in Dunbar & East Lothian"
  heading="Cremation"
  description="Arranging a cremation from Dunbar: which crematorium, how long the service lasts, what happens to the ashes, and what it costs."
  standfirst="With a full service at the crematorium, at a church beforehand, or somewhere that meant something to them."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    Cremation is now the choice of around three quarters of families in Scotland. It does
    not mean a smaller or lesser funeral — the service can be exactly as full as you want
    it to be, and it opens up more choice about when and where to hold it.
  </p>

  <h2>Which crematorium</h2>
  <p>
    Houndwood, in Berwickshire, is the closest to Dunbar — a converted 1830s church about
    twenty-five minutes down the A1, and quite unlike a conventional crematorium. Its one
    real drawback is access: it stands on a hill and is difficult for anyone with mobility
    problems, so it does not suit every family.
  </p>
  <p>
    East Lothian Crematorium at Musselburgh is level throughout and about forty minutes
    away, and is the one most families here use. Some choose an Edinburgh crematorium, and
    families further into Berwickshire sometimes prefer Borders Crematorium near Melrose.
    You are not tied to the nearest one.
  </p>
  <p>
    We have written up each of them — the chapel, how many people it seats, the parking,
    the music systems, how long you get, and what the surroundings are actually like — in
    our <a href="/directory/crematoria/">crematorium directory</a>. It is worth a look if
    you are trying to picture the day.
  </p>

  <h2>How the service works</h2>
  <p>
    Crematoria allocate a fixed time slot, usually 30 or 45 minutes including arriving and
    leaving. That is enough for a full service with music, readings and a eulogy, but it
    is a real limit and it is worth knowing about in advance.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you want more time, there are two straightforward answers: book a double slot,
    which most crematoria allow, or hold the main service at a church or at our funeral
    home and go to the crematorium afterwards for a short committal. Plenty of families
    in East Lothian do the second.
  </p>

  <Callout title="You do not have to go at all">
    <p>
      Some families hold the service somewhere else entirely and let us take the person to
      the crematorium separately, with nobody present. It is a perfectly dignified choice
      and more common than people think.{' '}
      <a href="/funeral-services/direct-cremation/">More about direct cremation</a>.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Music, words and photographs</h2>
  <p>
    Every local crematorium can play recorded music, and most have a visual system for
    photographs or a slideshow. Some can record or livestream the service for family who
    cannot travel — worth asking about if relatives are abroad. We will handle the
    booking and get your music to them in the right format well beforehand.
  </p>

  <h2>The paperwork</h2>
  <p>
    Cremation requires more forms than burial, and we complete all of them. If the death
    has been reported to the Procurator Fiscal, we will need their clearance first, which
    can add a few days. We will keep you posted rather than leave you wondering.
  </p>

  <h2>The ashes</h2>
  <p>
    The ashes are usually ready within a few days. We will collect them and keep them
    here for as long as you need — there is no time limit and no charge for holding them.
    Some families collect them the same week; some take a year to decide.
  </p>
  <p>You can then:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Take them home</li>
    <li>Bury them in a family lair or a garden of remembrance</li>
    <li>Scatter them somewhere that mattered to the person</li>
    <li>Divide them between family members</li>
    <li>Have some kept in jewellery or set in glass</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you want to scatter on land you do not own, ask the landowner first. For the John
    Muir Way, the beaches or the country parks, we can tell you who to speak to.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Our fee is on our{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/standardised-price-list/">Standardised Price List</a>. The
    crematorium's own fee sits on top and is paid to them, not to us — we pass it on
    exactly as charged. Crematorium fees vary and are usually reviewed each April.
  </p>
  <p>There is no cremation fee in Scotland for anyone under 18.</p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      To talk it through, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/directory/crematoria/">Crematoria across the east of Scotland</a></li>
    <li><a href="/funeral-services/direct-cremation/">Direct cremation</a></li>
    <li><a href="/guides/burial-or-cremation/">Choosing between burial and cremation</a></li>
  </ul>
</Page>
